[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2753888919","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104634#issuecomment-2753888919","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104634","id":2753888919,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kJQKX","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T10:17:24Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T11:08:54Z","body":"Vararg reductions (like MIN / MAX) are nice, I agree.\r\nBut it's also not super common to have something like this in a codebase / language, making it maybe somewhat of a surprise to readers that aren't as familiar with vararg functions.\r\nSo in the end i feel kind of indifferent about this feature. Perhaps it would be better motivated if there more functions that would benefit from using it?\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2753888919/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754103083","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104634#issuecomment-2754103083","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104634","id":2754103083,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kKEcr","user":{"login":"ibrahn","id":24498832,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NDk4ODMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24498832?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn","html_url":"https://github.com/ibrahn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T11:35:45Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T11:35:45Z","body":"A good point. Though possibly understating its prevalence a bit.\r\nOff the top of my head, Python, JavaScript, Lua, PHP and of course GDScript all have variadic `max`/`min` as their builtin/standard library versions. The C++ standard library has a variant that takes an initializer list, as there was already a three argument template (taking a comparison function).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754103083/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754136121","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104634#issuecomment-2754136121","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104634","id":2754136121,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kKMg5","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T11:50:13Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T11:50:13Z","body":"From a quick look, I found 22 occurrences of `MAX(.*, MAX(` and 16 of `MIN(.*, MIN(` (counting occurrences manually from the regex results as it's a pretty lazy one and also globs stuff like `MAX(a, b), MAX(c, d)` which are not relevant).\r\n\r\nSo it's a decent number to refactor but not showing a huge need either, so I'm likewise somewhat neutral about this addition. Is there any impact on binary size / performance from adding such variadic code?\r\n\r\nWe're also trending towards moving this kind of stuff to the `Math` namespace so this might be something to consider too (though I wouldn't suggest doing both at the same time, as the refactoring for usual `MAX(a, b)` cases will make the changes hard to review).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754136121/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754288456","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104634#issuecomment-2754288456","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104634","id":2754288456,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kKxtI","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T12:47:50Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T12:47:50Z","body":"> Is there any impact on binary size / performance from adding such variadic code?\r\n\r\nI wouldn't expect it since it should compile to the same binary code.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754288456/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754317806","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104634#issuecomment-2754317806","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104634","id":2754317806,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kK43u","user":{"login":"ibrahn","id":24498832,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NDk4ODMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24498832?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn","html_url":"https://github.com/ibrahn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T12:58:33Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T12:58:33Z","body":"At `-O1` and above I believe `MAX(a, b, c)` will produce the same assembly as the existing `MAX(MAX(a, b), c`.\r\nThere's always the compiler to pay though, however cheaply, so if it doesn't improve readability for anyone else I'm more than happy to live with `MAX(MAX())` :)\r\n\r\n`Math` namespace seems like a good home. I'm guessing they'd be lowercase `max`/`min` there? Those could exist alongside the current `MAX`/`MIN` and be swapped in as convenient.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754317806/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754647073","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104634#issuecomment-2754647073","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104634","id":2754647073,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kMJQh","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T14:32:38Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T14:32:38Z","body":"> `Math` namespace seems like a good home. I'm guessing they'd be lowercase `max`/`min` there? Those could exist alongside the current `MAX`/`MIN` and be swapped in as convenient.\r\n\r\nYeah, it would be lowercase.\r\nThe idea is to replace `MAX` / `MIN` entirely, analogously to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/69406 for `ABS`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754647073/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754663269","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104634#issuecomment-2754663269","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104634","id":2754663269,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kMNNl","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T14:37:24Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T14:37:24Z","body":"I'd say let's go with this PR as is, but adding the actual replacements of occurrences of `MIN(MIN(` and `MAX(MAX(`, so that we make use of the new feature consistently.\r\n\r\nIn a later PR we could look at moving `MIN` and `MAX` to `Math::min()` and `Math::max()`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2754663269/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755776854","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104634#issuecomment-2755776854","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104634","id":2755776854,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kQdFW","user":{"login":"ibrahn","id":24498832,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NDk4ODMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24498832?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn","html_url":"https://github.com/ibrahn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibrahn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T21:22:39Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T21:22:39Z","body":"Ran into a bit of a problem with the Xcode builds.\r\nA header (`NSObjCRuntime.h`) which defines `MIN`/`MAX` macros is included after `core/typedefs.h` and prevents the template versions being called correctly. (I think this means that these builds are not currently using our existing templates either).\r\nTried the following fix:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/eecca3d9d04092b5b04d2da4bfe5a4704c6949e9/core/typedefs.h#L122-L124\r\nbut it's still failing on the iOS build with:\r\n```\r\nError: ./core/math/color.h:144:40: error: too many arguments provided to function-like macro invocation [1]\r\n                const float MaxChannel = MAX(_r, _g, _b, kMinVal);\r\n                                                      ^\r\n/Applications/Xcode_15.4.app/Contents/Developer/Platforms/iPhoneOS.platform/Developer/SDKs/iPhoneOS17.5.sdk/System/Library/Frameworks/Foundation.framework/Headers/NSObjCRuntime.h:684:13: note: macro 'MAX' defined here [1]\r\n     #define MAX(A,B) __NSMAX_IMPL__(A,B,__COUNTER__)\r\n             ^\r\nIn file included from platform/ios/key_mapping_ios.mm:33:\r\nIn file included from ./core/templates/hash_map.h:34:\r\nIn file included from ./core/templates/hashfuncs.h:35:\r\nError: ./core/math/color.h:144:28:{144:28-144:31}: error: address of overloaded function 'MAX' does not match required type 'float' [2]\r\n                const float MaxChannel = MAX(_r, _g, _b, kMinVal);\r\n                                          ^~~\r\n```\r\nWhich I think makes this a dead one for now. Possibly to revisit if min/max moves to the Godot `Math` namespace later.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755776854/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]